Trazo License (source-available, non-commercial) - English translation

Copyright (c) 2026 Antidecn. All rights reserved except those expressly
granted in this license.

"The Software" means Trazo: its source code, installer, published binaries,
logo, icons and every other file in this repository.

1. What you may do

   Free of charge and without asking for permission, you may:

   a) View, read and download the source code and the published installers.
   b) Install and use the Trazo program as a tool, including at work.
   c) Fork the repository on GitHub.
   d) Build, run, debug and modify the code on your own computer to study
      it, learn from it, find bugs or test changes.
   e) Propose changes to the original repository (issues and pull requests).

2. What you may not do

   a) Use the Software, or any part of its code, for profit or commercial
      purposes. This includes, among other things: selling it; charging for
      downloading, installing or supporting it; including it in a paid
      product or service; offering it with ads, subscriptions or in-app
      purchases; or using it to build a product that competes with Trazo.
   b) Distribute the Software, or a modified version, under a different
      name, logo or author, or present it as your own work.
   c) Remove or change this LICENSE file, the copyright notice or the
      credit to the author.
   d) Use the name "Trazo" or its logo to identify another product, or in a
      way that suggests the author endorses a version that is not theirs.

   If you publish a fork or share a modified version, it must keep the name
   Trazo, credit the original author with a link to
   https://github.com/antidecn, include this license unchanged, state
   clearly that it is a modified version, and it may not be used for
   commercial purposes.

3. Contributions

   By submitting a change to the original repository (for example, a pull
   request), you allow the author to include it in Trazo and to distribute
   it under this license or any license the author chooses in the future.

4. Additional permissions

   Any use not allowed by this license, including commercial use, requires
   the author's prior written permission.

5. Termination

   If you breach this license, the permissions it grants you end
   automatically.

6. No warranty

   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the
   extent permitted by law, the author is not liable for any damage or loss
   arising from its use.

7. Language

   This English text is a translation for reference only. If the two
   versions differ, the Spanish version prevails.
